From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Miguel Salinas <mikeys@me.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:11:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(durable): settings.retry.keepRetried leaves retried
 attempts out of the transcript

Every failed attempt is appended as a pi.assistant entry, also when the run
asks again and then answers. Context derivation skips them, but a host that
shows or serves the conversation's history had to recognize and hide the
superseded failures itself, or retry outside the Harness to keep them out.

With settings.retry.keepRetried: false, a failed attempt that is asked again (a
retry, an overflow that starts a compaction, an interrupted request or poll)
appends no entry and records only its usage in pi.usage. The transcript holds
the attempt that answered, or the last one that failed; pi.live.generation
still shows the retry's error during the backoff. Default true, unchanged.
